# .trivyignore - findings reviewed and accepted.
#
# One block per finding: what it is, why it is not fixable here, why it is not
# reachable (or why the exposure is accepted), when to revisit. Cleared
# waivers are deleted, not kept - git log has the history.
#
# Full rewrite 2026-11-17 against upstream 2.5.11 (issue #42). Every entry
# below was re-verified against the 2.5.11 tree; everything that no longer
# matches was removed. Default calendar revisit for everything: 2027-01.
#
# Deployment assumptions the "REVERT IF" markers guard: no gRPC monitor, no
# MSSQL monitor using Azure AD / Entra authentication, no Cloudflare Tunnel
# monitor, dashboard not reachable from untrusted networks, and every
# MySQL/MariaDB endpoint we connect to (monitor targets and the app's own
# database) sits on our own trusted segment.

# ============================================================================
# uptime-kuma npm deps. `npm ci` installs package-lock.json verbatim, so a
# same-tag rebuild never moves these - only an upstream lockfile change does.
# Overriding the pins downstream would be a source fork, which this repo does
# not do (see oss-mirror-build/README.md).
# ============================================================================

# minimatch 9.0.3 ReDoS (HIGH, DoS). Needs an attacker-controlled glob
# pattern. No require("glob") / require("minimatch") in server/, src/ or
# extra/ at 2.5.11; the only consumers are transitive, on literal paths.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# glob 10.3.16 CLI command injection (HIGH). Only the `glob -c <cmd>` CLI form
# is affected; nothing in uptime-kuma spawns the glob CLI.
CVE-2025-64756

# node-tar 6.2.1 - extraction path-traversal / hardlink / symlink family,
# gzip-bomb DoS (59873, NVD CRITICAL, GHSA CVSS 7.5 A:H), tar.replace() loop
# (59874) and long-path DoS (73566). Fix floor 7.5.21, a major jump from the
# `~6.2.1` pin.
# Re-verified at 2.5.11: the only require("tar") sites are
# extra/download-dist.js:3 (install-time) and extra/release/lib.mjs:5
# (release tooling). Neither is in the release image's runtime graph.
# REVERT IF: a runtime require("tar") appears in server/.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566

# protobufjs 7.2.6 - RCE via crafted .proto (41242, CVSS 9.8) and the
# follow-on family (44289, 44290, 44291, 44293, 48712). Fix floors up to
# 7.6.1, outside the `~7.2.6` pin.
# Single call site: server/monitor-types/grpc.js decodes gRPC responses
# against a user-supplied .proto. We run no gRPC monitor, so the decode path
# is never invoked. Even with one, the .proto is admin-supplied.
# REVERT IF: a gRPC monitor is added - 41242 and 44291 are RCE shapes.
CVE-2026-41242
CVE-2026-44289
CVE-2026-44290
CVE-2026-44291
CVE-2026-44293
CVE-2026-48712

# @grpc/grpc-js 1.8.22 - three server-side bugs:
#   48068  malformed request crashes a gRPC server (DoS)
#   48069  malformed compressed message crashes client or server (DoS)
#   101916 getAuthContext() treats an unauthorized peer certificate as
#          authorized when the SERVER runs with requireClientCertificate=false
# uptime-kuma uses grpc-js as a client only (server/monitor-types/grpc.js);
# no grpc.Server is created anywhere at 2.5.11, so getAuthContext on a server
# credential is never reached. 48069's client path needs a gRPC monitor
# pointed at a hostile endpoint; we run none.
# REVERT IF: a gRPC monitor is added (48069), or upstream starts a gRPC server.
CVE-2026-48068
CVE-2026-48069
CVE-2026-101916

# lodash 4.17.23 (nested under redbean-node; top-level is already fixed) -
# _.template imports key injection (HIGH). redbean-node uses lodash for
# utility functions only; _.template is never invoked.
CVE-2026-4800

# jsonata 2.2.0 - arbitrary code execution via a crafted JSONata EXPRESSION
# (77414, 77415, both CRITICAL). Fix 2.2.1, upstream pins exactly 2.2.0.
# (77413 and 52746 cleared with the 2.2.0 bump and were removed.)
# The attacker-controlled input is the expression itself, not the data it
# evaluates. Every call site at 2.5.11 takes the expression from an
# admin-configured monitor field:
#   server/monitor-types/mongodb.js:27   jsonata(monitor.jsonPath)
#   server/monitor-types/mqtt.js:79,106  jsonata(monitor.jsonPath)
#   src/util.js:409,444                  jsonPath / jsonQueryExpression
# All set through the authenticated EditMonitor UI. Only the probe RESPONSE
# is untrusted, and evaluating data with an already-parsed expression is not
# the vulnerable path.
# REVERT IF: an expression ever becomes derivable from probe output, an API
# payload, or any unauthenticated input. Re-grep the call sites on each bump.
CVE-2026-77414
CVE-2026-77415

# nodemailer 7.0.13 - four findings, all outside the `~7.0.13` pin (fix
# floors 8.0.8 to 10.0.6, several majors out):
#   82659 (= GHSA-p6gq-j5cr-w38f) message-level `raw` bypasses
#         disableFileAccess / disableUrlAccess. The smtp provider never sets
#         `raw`.
#   82662 lib/fetch disables TLS verification for OAuth2 token requests.
#         server/notification-providers/smtp.js uses plain user/pass auth and
#         configures no OAuth2 / xoauth2, so lib/fetch is never called.
#   GHSA-2x7j-588g-ccc2, GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j  quadratic addressparser
#         (event-loop DoS from a huge To/Cc/Bcc/From value). The only address
#         inputs are smtpFrom/smtpTo/smtpCC/smtpBCC (smtp.js:94-97), all
#         admin-configured notification settings. No address is ever taken
#         from probe output or unauthenticated input; nothing else calls
#         addressparser.
# REVERT IF: OAuth2 SMTP auth is added (82662), or any address field becomes
# templated from monitor/heartbeat data.
CVE-2026-82659
CVE-2026-82662
GHSA-2x7j-588g-ccc2
GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j

# liquidjs 10.26.0 - three template-author DoS bugs, fixes 10.27.1 / 10.27.2,
# outside the `~10.26.0` pin:
#   55575  `pop` filter skips memoryLimit accounting
#   61556  infinite loop in `strip_html`
#   69222  `join` / `array_to_sentence_string` undercount memory and can
#          crash the process
# The only Liquid engine is server/notification-providers/
# notification-provider.js:76, rendering notification templates. uptime-kuma
# sets no memoryLimit/renderLimit at all (so 55575 has no budget to bypass),
# and none of strip_html, join or array_to_sentence_string appears in any
# shipped template (grepped across 2.5.11). Reaching any of them needs an
# admin to hand-write the filter into a custom template; the ceiling is then
# a stalled or crashed notification path - no code execution, no data
# exposure.
# REVERT IF: one of these filters appears in a shipped template, or upstream
# starts setting a liquidjs memoryLimit.
CVE-2026-55575
CVE-2026-61556
CVE-2026-69222

# axios 0.32.0 - two prototype-pollution gadgets, fixes 0.33.0 / 0.34.0,
# outside the `~0.32.0` pin. axios IS the HTTP-monitor and notification
# engine, so both rest on the exploit precondition, not on the library being
# unused:
#   67320 (= GHSA-gcfj-64vw-6mp9) the Node adapter reads config.proxy off a
#         polluted Object.prototype. Needs a request interceptor returning a
#         plain-object clone; there is still no interceptors.request.use in
#         server/, src/ or extra/ at 2.5.11. Proxying uses explicit agents
#         from server/proxy.js, never config.proxy.
#   101909 toFormData honours inherited serialization options. This path IS
#         live (sms-planet.js and goalert.js post multipart/form-data through
#         axios), but the advisory requires a separate, already-present
#         prototype-pollution primitive in the same process. Without one
#         there is nothing to inherit; with one, the process is already
#         compromised by stronger means.
# REVERT IF: any interceptors.request.use appears, or a prototype-pollution
# CVE lands in a server-side dependency. Grep on every upstream bump.
CVE-2026-67320
CVE-2026-101909

# ws 8.19.0 - memory-exhaustion DoS from small WebSocket fragments (HIGH).
# Fix 8.21.0. Only the top-level `ws@~8.19.0` pin is affected; its only call
# site is server/monitor-types/websocket-upgrade.js, an OUTBOUND client
# toward an operator-configured probe target. No server-side ws listener.
# REVERT IF: ws is used to accept inbound connections.
CVE-2026-48779

# @azure/msal-node 5.6.0 (via mssql -> tedious -> @azure/identity) - origin
# validation error in the authorization-code flow can disclose parameters to
# an attacker-controlled endpoint (HIGH, C:H). Fix 7.1.0, outside identity's
# `^5.1.0` range; needs upstream to move mssql/tedious.
# uptime-kuma calls msal only indirectly, through tedious, and only when an
# MSSQL monitor's connection string selects Azure AD / Entra authentication.
# The authorization-code flow is an interactive browser login that tedious
# never drives. Plain SQL auth (the only MSSQL mode we would use) never
# invokes msal, even though tedious may load the module.
# REVERT IF: an MSSQL monitor with Azure AD / Entra authentication is added.
CVE-2026-109461

# mysql2 3.11.5 - a server can force `mysql_clear_password` without TLS, so
# the configured password goes out in plaintext (HIGH). Fix 3.22.0, far
# outside the `~3.11.5` pin; upstream lockfile refresh only.
# Honest exposure - this is a confidentiality bug with a real path, accepted
# on trust boundary rather than on the code being unused. Call sites at
# 2.5.11: embedded-mariadb.js (local unix socket), setup-database.js
# (one-time wizard), database.js (app DB), monitor-types/mysql.js (arbitrary
# operator-configured endpoint - the one that matters).
# Accepted because every MySQL/MariaDB endpoint this instance talks to is on
# our own segment: no hostile server to send the downgrade, no on-path
# position to MITM it. Blast radius if that breaks: one monitor's DB
# credential, not the dashboard.
# REVERT IF: a MySQL/MariaDB monitor is pointed outside our trusted segment,
# or the app database moves across an untrusted network. Re-read this entry
# before adding any MySQL monitor.
GHSA-3f6p-5ww8-9rcr

# ============================================================================
# cloudflared (installed from Cloudflare's apt repo, 2026.11.0 at this
# rewrite). Idle unless a Cloudflare Tunnel monitor is configured; we
# configure none. We cannot bump what it vendors without Cloudflare
# rebuilding the .deb. All earlier cloudflared waivers (Go stdlib waves,
# x/crypto/ssh, grpc-go) cleared with 2026.11.0 and were removed.
# ============================================================================

# golang.org/x/net v0.61.0 - x/net/html DoS via crafted HTML input (HIGH).
# Fix 0.62.0. cloudflared does not parse HTML in any path we could reach, and
# the binary is never executed here (no tunnel, no ingress config).
# Our own healthcheck binary is stdlib-only and does not carry x/net.
# REVERT IF: a Cloudflare Tunnel monitor is configured.
CVE-2026-78661
